fof_version: '0.1'
type: enemy
id: bought_sergeant
name: Sergeant-at-Arms
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 0.1.0
enemy:
  tier: named
  attack_modifier: 2
  armor: light
  techniques:
  - hold_the_terms
  special: HOLD THE TERMS — once per scene, the sergeant states the contract's boundary aloud.
    Every Blade in earshot immediately behaves as though the boundary is where the sergeant
    just said it is, whatever they believed a moment ago.
  description: The one reading the room instead of the target. Sergeants of the Bought carry
    the contract itself in a case chained at the hip and produce it more readily than steel
    — which lands strangely in Val'loh, where the written word belongs to the Church and a
    chained case of it is either blasphemy or a very expensive dispensation. Nobody at the
    gate is going to ask which tonight.
  disposition: Reads first, fights second, and would genuinely rather not.
  first_target: Whoever is closest to breaking the contract's boundary.
  triggers:
  - Opens by naming the contract's terms aloud. This is not a bluff; it is how the company
    works.
  - Spends Hold the Terms when the party splits, to keep the Blades from following anyone
    past the line.
  morale: Surrenders the field the moment the contract is void — payment withdrawn, terms
    broken by the employer, or the named target gone. Will say so out loud and expect to be
    believed.
  organization: One per four Blades. Four of them are in Rekuzan.
  notes: 'TR breakdown: offense(+2 → 4) + durability(Resolve 3) + armor(light → 1) + techniques(1)
    = 9.


    MODULE RESKIN (Oraga Night). Flavour fields only — description and organization. Tier,
    resolve, attack_modifier, armor, techniques and special are the Bestiary''s and must stay
    identical to enemies/bought_sergeant.fof; a test asserts it. The Bestiary files stay setting-agnostic
    (B9), which is why the Val''loh colour lives here instead.'
  negotiation: Wants the contract satisfied or voided; either ends the fight. Shifts for proof
    the employer has broken terms. Honours any deal that lets the company withdraw with its
    fee and its reputation.
  resolve: 3
created_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
